Sure. Before ISP you might have:
```java
interface Vehicle { void drive(); void fly(); void sail(); }
class Car implements Vehicle { public void drive() {} public void fly() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(); } public void sail() { throw new UnsupportedOperationException(); } }
```
After applying ISP you split it:
```java
interface Drivable { void drive(); }
interface Flyable { void fly(); }
interface Sailable { void sail(); }
class Car implements Drivable { public void drive() {} }
```
Now `Car` only implements what it actually supports, and no one is forced to handle `UnsupportedOperationException`.

