The common pitfall is recomputing the character set from scratch each time you move the left pointer, which makes the inner work linear in the window size. To achieve O(n), maintain a hash map that records the last index where each character appeared; when you encounter a repeat, jump the left edge directly to max(previous left, last index + 1). This way each character is processed at most twice—once when the right edge reaches it and possibly once when the left edge skips over it.

